# Go core (`services/`)

## Layout

- One module under `services/core` (or `services/core/` binary at `cmd/wichat`).
- Domain packages with **narrow exports**; HTTP/WebSocket/gRPC live in `internal/transport/` or `internal/<module>/api`.
- No business logic in `main`. Cross-module calls go through interfaces defined in the consumer package.

## Errors & API

- Wrap errors with context (`fmt.Errorf("workspace: create: %w", err)`).
- Never leak internal errors to clients; map to HTTP status + safe message per SDD §13.
- Context-first: pass `context.Context` on all I/O boundaries.

## Tests

- Table-driven unit tests; `testify` for assertions when it clarifies.
- Integration tests with **testcontainers** for Postgres/Redis when touching persistence.
- Target ~90% coverage on core domain packages over time — not on generated or thin wiring.

## Dependencies

- Prefer stdlib; new modules need a one-line justification in PR description.
- AGPL-compatible licenses only unless explicitly approved.
